{% doc %}
  Handles messages sent by a client via `subscription.send(...)` on the
  `pos_websocket` channel. Re-runs the exact same authorization check as
  `subscribed.liquid` (membership can change after a client subscribed —
  e.g. a room going from public back to... it can't currently, but a
  member being removed is plausible in an app-specific override — and a
  client could otherwise call `send` on a room_id it never actually
  subscribed to) and, unless rejected, broadcasts it to every current
  subscriber of `room_id` via channel_send_message.

  The client's payload is never relayed verbatim: `user_id` is always
  overwritten with the sender's real id, so subscribers can trust who a
  message came from. Everything else in the payload is client-supplied —
  treat it as untrusted input. Echoing 'false' suppresses ActionCable's
  default rebroadcast of the raw payload, which would let a client claim
  any identity it likes.

  Also publishes `websocket_message_received` via the core Event System so
  consuming apps can react (persist it, moderate it, fan it out elsewhere)
  by adding a consumer under lib/consumers/websocket_message_received/,
  without touching this file. Override this file directly (Module Override
  System) if you need to reject/transform messages before they broadcast.
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  # Always suppress the default raw rebroadcast; authorized messages are
  # re-sent below with a server-stamped user_id.
  echo 'false'

  assign room_id = context.params.room_id

  if context.current_user != blank
    function authorized = 'modules/websocket/queries/rooms/authorized', room_id: room_id, user_id: context.current_user.id

    if authorized
      assign payload = context.params | hash_merge: user_id: context.current_user.id
      graphql _result = 'modules/websocket/messages/broadcast', room_id: room_id, payload: payload

      assign event_payload = {
        "room_id": room_id,
        "user_id": context.current_user.id,
        "payload": payload
      }
      function _ = 'modules/core/commands/events/publish', type: 'websocket_message_received', object: event_payload, delay: null, max_attempts: null
    endif
  endif
%}
